/* =====================================================================
   Torrent 2000 -- "CCCP" skin, NORMAL variant
   Soviet-constructivist propaganda-poster aesthetic. Not a real OS, so the
   reference here is real Soviet propaganda poster art (Rodchenko, El
   Lissitzky, Civil-War-era recruitment posters), not a screenshot of a
   dead operating system. Flat, high-contrast, silkscreened fields; thick
   square-cut ink borders; bold sans type. No gradients, no soft shading.

   PALETTE DERIVATION -- this is not an invented palette. Four real posters
   (Wikimedia Commons, public domain / PD-old) were downloaded and pixel-
   sampled with PIL: a red/black/cream clustering + per-cluster median over
   a downsampled copy of each image (avoids anti-aliased-edge noise from a
   single hand-picked coordinate). See scratchpad CHARTE_CCCP.md for the
   full method, per-image measurements, and the two small scripts used.

     measured poster red     -> #D84E2F  (avg of two posters' red clusters:
                                 #D84F3B "Krasny Podarok" rocket, #D94E23
                                 El Lissitzky's red wedge)
     measured poster black   -> #202120  (avg of the same two posters'
                                 black-ground clusters)
     measured poster cream   -> #EAE0CA  (avg of three posters' aged-paper
                                 clusters) -- within 8/255 per channel of
                                 the title bar's ALREADY-FIXED caption text
                                 color #F2E4C4 (theme_manager.py), so that
                                 fixed value is reused here rather than
                                 re-derived: measurement independently
                                 confirms it belongs to the same parchment
                                 family, it doesn't contradict it.

   TOKENS (hex, named)
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
     bg               #161616   canvas the poster board sits on (darker
                                 than the measured board itself -- the
                                 canvas reads as the wall behind the
                                 mounted poster, not the poster paper)
     surface          #202120   panel / card -- the measured poster-black
                                 value itself, used directly
     border           #EAE0CA   parchment ink-line -- measured poster cream
     text             #F2E4C4   parchment cream -- ALREADY FIXED (title bar
                                 caption text, theme_manager.py); measured
                                 poster cream (#EAE0CA) confirms the family
     text-muted       #9F9889   dulled parchment -- measured cream, value
                                 scaled down ~32% in HSV (keeps the same
                                 hue/warmth, just dimmer, not a different
                                 invented tone)
     accent (red)     #D84E2F   primary interactive red -- measured poster
                                 red, used directly
     accent-hover     #D4AF37   gold -- ALREADY FIXED (title bar hover gold,
                                 theme_manager.py). Every hover state here
                                 resolves red-becomes-gold, same as hovering
                                 the real caption buttons.
     danger           #A31515   destructive-action red -- ALREADY FIXED
                                 (title bar close/minmax button fill,
                                 theme_manager.py) -- the one button allowed
                                 to BE red instead of merely bordered by it
                                 uses the exact red the window chrome itself
                                 is built from.

   Utility shades (not part of the named palette, purely structural, no
   real-world poster referent -- a disabled control or a hover tint has no
   equivalent in 1920s silkscreen art):
     inset            #0D0D0D   recessed field background (carved-in look)
     hover-surface    #2A2A2A   lightened surface, generic hover fill
     alt-row          #1A1A1A   table alternating row
     disabled-border  #3A3A3A   neutral (deliberately NOT warm -- a
                                 disabled control should read "switched
                                 off," not a dimmer parchment tone)
     disabled-text    #6E6E6E

   Corner radius: 0px everywhere, echoing window_corner_radius=0 for CCCP
   in theme_manager.py (square window chrome -> square controls).

   The title bar (solid red caption, hammer-and-sickle close button) is NOT
   drawn by this stylesheet -- see ui/widgets/app_title_bar.py and
   ui/theme/theme_manager.py. Two theme-specific mechanics live outside QSS
   entirely: downloading is blocked while this theme is active
   (engine/session_manager.py) and sharing counts for 3x toward the level
   (stats/leveling.py).
   ===================================================================== */

* {
    font-family: "Arial", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    font-size: 9pt;
}

QMainWindow, QWidget#centralWidget, QDialog {
    background-color: #161616;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

QWidget {
    background-color: #161616;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- Tabs */

QTabWidget::pane {
    border: 2px solid #EAE0CA;
    background-color: #161616;
    top: -1px;
}

QTabWidget#mainTabs::pane {
    border-top: none;
    top: 0px;
}

QTabBar::tab {
    background-color: #202120;
    border: 2px solid #EAE0CA;
    border-bottom: none;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 5px 16px;
    margin-right: 1px;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    font-weight: bold;
}

QTabBar::tab:hover:!selected {
    background-color: #2A2A2A;
    color: #D4AF37;
    border-color: #D4AF37;
}

QTabBar::tab:selected {
    background-color: #161616;
    border-color: #EAE0CA;
    border-bottom: 3px solid #D84E2F;
    margin-top: 0px;
    color: #D84E2F;
}

QTabBar::tab:!selected {
    margin-top: 2px;
}

QTabBar::tab:disabled {
    color: #6E6E6E;
    border-color: #3A3A3A;
}

QTabBar::tab:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline-offset: -3px;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------ GroupBox */

QGroupBox {
    border: 2px solid #EAE0CA;
    border-top: 4px solid #D84E2F;
    border-radius: 0px;
    margin-top: 10px;
    padding-top: 10px;
    background-color: #202120;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #D84E2F;
}

QGroupBox::title {
    subcontrol-origin: margin;
    left: 10px;
    top: -2px;
    padding: 0 6px;
    background-color: #202120;
    color: #D84E2F;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------- Buttons */

QPushButton {
    background-color: #202120;
    border: 2px solid #EAE0CA;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    min-height: 18px;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    font-weight: bold;
}

QPushButton:hover:!pressed {
    background-color: #2A2A2A;
    border: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    color: #D4AF37;
}

QPushButton:pressed {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    border: 2px solid #D84E2F;
    color: #D84E2F;
}

QPushButton:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline-offset: 2px;
}

QPushButton:default {
    border-width: 3px;
    border-color: #D84E2F;
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

QPushButton:disabled {
    background-color: #202120;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

/* The one button allowed to BE red instead of merely bordered by it --
   removing a torrent is exactly the kind of decisive action this theme's
   red accent is reserved for. Fill and hover match the real title bar's
   close/minmax button colors exactly (see theme_manager.py). */
QPushButton#dangerButton {
    background-color: #A31515;
    border: 2px solid #EAE0CA;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 2px 10px;
    min-height: 16px;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    font-weight: bold;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:hover:!pressed {
    background-color: #D4AF37;
    border: 2px solid #F2E4C4;
    color: #161616;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:pressed {
    background-color: #6E0E0E;
    border: 2px solid #EAE0CA;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #F2E4C4;
    outline-offset: 2px;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:disabled {
    background-color: #3A1414;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------- Text input */

QLineEdit, QSpinBox, QAbstractSpinBox {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 2px 4px;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    selection-background-color: #D84E2F;
    selection-color: #F2E4C4;
}

QLineEdit:hover, QSpinBox:hover, QAbstractSpinBox:hover {
    border: 2px solid #D84E2F;
}

QLineEdit:focus, QSpinBox:focus, QAbstractSpinBox:focus {
    border: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline-offset: 1px;
}

QLineEdit:disabled, QSpinBox:disabled, QAbstractSpinBox:disabled {
    background-color: #161616;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-button, QAbstractSpinBox::down-button {
    subcontrol-origin: border;
    width: 16px;
    background-color: #202120;
    border-left: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-button {
    subcontrol-position: top right;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-button:hover, QAbstractSpinBox::down-button:hover {
    background-color: #2A2A2A;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::down-button {
    subcontrol-position: bottom right;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-arrow {
    width: 0;
    height: 0;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-bottom: 4px solid #F2E4C4;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::down-arrow {
    width: 0;
    height: 0;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-top: 4px solid #F2E4C4;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-arrow:disabled, QAbstractSpinBox::down-arrow:disabled {
    border-bottom-color: #6E6E6E;
    border-top-color: #6E6E6E;
}

/* -------------------------------------------------------------- Combo */

QComboBox {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 2px 4px;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

QComboBox:hover {
    border: 2px solid #D84E2F;
}

QComboBox:focus {
    border: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline-offset: 1px;
}

QComboBox:disabled {
    background-color: #161616;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

QComboBox::drop-down {
    subcontrol-origin: padding;
    subcontrol-position: right;
    width: 20px;
    background-color: #202120;
    border-left: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QComboBox::drop-down:hover {
    background-color: #2A2A2A;
}

QComboBox::down-arrow {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    image: none;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-top: 4px solid #F2E4C4;
}

QComboBox::down-arrow:disabled {
    border-top: 4px solid #6E6E6E;
}

/* Popup list -- the currently-selected/current item must never end up
   rendering with text the same color as its own background (the known
   Windows-7-family bug this rebuild must not repeat). selection-background-
   color/selection-color set the view's palette Highlight/HighlightedText
   roles directly (verified by introspecting view.palette() after this
   stylesheet is applied: Highlight resolves to #D84E2F, HighlightedText to
   #F2E4C4) -- that is the primary, always-correct mechanism. The ::item
   rules below are redundant belt-and-suspenders coverage for the native
   Windows styles this offscreen test harness cannot exercise (verified:
   in the offscreen/Fusion combination used for automated testing here, a
   combo box popup's pre-highlighted current item doesn't repaint from
   EITHER mechanism without a live compositor -- confirmed project-wide,
   not specific to this file, by testing the already-rebuilt win95.qss
   sibling with the same idiom). Either way, text and fill are never the
   same color in any state below. */
QComboBox QAbstractItemView {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    border: 2px solid #D84E2F;
    outline: none;
    padding: 2px;
    selection-background-color: #D84E2F;
    selection-color: #F2E4C4;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item {
    padding: 4px 8px;
    min-height: 20px;
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    border: none;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item:hover {
    background-color: #D84E2F;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item:selected {
    background-color: #D84E2F;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------ Checkbox */

QCheckBox {
    color: #F2E4C4;
    spacing: 6px;
}

QCheckBox:disabled {
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

QCheckBox::indicator {
    width: 13px;
    height: 13px;
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:hover {
    border: 2px solid #D4AF37;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline-offset: 1px;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked {
    background-color: #D84E2F;
    border: 2px solid #D84E2F;
    image: url(theme:checkmark.png);
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked:hover {
    background-color: #D4AF37;
    border: 2px solid #D4AF37;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:disabled {
    background-color: #202120;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked:disabled {
    background-color: #6E6E6E;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
}

/* -------------------------------------------------------------- Slider */

QSlider::groove:horizontal {
    height: 4px;
    background-color: #3A3A3A;
    border: 2px solid #0D0D0D;
}

QSlider::groove:horizontal:disabled {
    background-color: #2A2A2A;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal {
    width: 14px;
    margin: -6px 0;
    background-color: #D84E2F;
    border: 2px solid #EAE0CA;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:hover {
    background-color: #D4AF37;
    border: 2px solid #F2E4C4;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:pressed {
    background-color: #D4AF37;
    border: 2px solid #FFFFFF;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline-offset: 1px;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:disabled {
    background-color: #6E6E6E;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------- Tables and trees */

QTableWidget, QTreeWidget {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    alternate-background-color: #1A1A1A;
    gridline-color: #3A3A3A;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    selection-background-color: #D84E2F;
    selection-color: #F2E4C4;
    outline: none;
}

QTableWidget::item, QTreeWidget::item {
    padding: 2px;
}

QTableWidget::item:hover, QTreeWidget::item:hover {
    background-color: #2A1414;
}

QTableWidget::item:selected, QTreeWidget::item:selected {
    background-color: #D84E2F;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

QHeaderView::section {
    background-color: #202120;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
    padding: 3px 6px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #D84E2F;
}

QHeaderView::section:hover {
    color: #D4AF37;
    border-color: #D4AF37;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------- ListBox */

QListWidget {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    outline: none;
}

QListWidget::item {
    padding: 4px 6px;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
}

QListWidget::item:hover {
    background-color: #2A1414;
    border-left: 3px solid #D4AF37;
}

QListWidget::item:selected {
    background-color: #D84E2F;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    border-left: 3px solid #D4AF37;
}

QListWidget::item:selected:!active {
    background-color: #6E0E0E;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ Menu */
/* Context menus (right-click on the Downloads/Share tables) need to look
   like part of the same poster, not fall back to native Windows chrome. */

QMenu {
    background-color: #202120;
    border: 2px solid #EAE0CA;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    padding: 3px;
}

QMenu::item {
    background-color: transparent;
    padding: 5px 24px 5px 16px;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
}

QMenu::item:selected {
    background-color: #D84E2F;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    border-left: 3px solid #D4AF37;
}

QMenu::item:disabled {
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

QMenu::separator {
    height: 2px;
    background-color: #D4AF37;
    margin: 4px 8px;
}

QMenu::icon {
    padding-left: 6px;
}

/* --------------------------------------------------------- ProgressBar */

/* The "People's Progress" -- red filling on a dark groove. */
QProgressBar {
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    text-align: center;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    font-weight: bold;
}

QProgressBar::chunk {
    background-color: #D84E2F;
    margin: 1px;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------- Misc chrome */

QLabel {
    background: transparent;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

QLabel:disabled {
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

QSplitter::handle {
    background-color: #161616;
}

QSplitter::handle:hover {
    background-color: #D4AF37;
}

QScrollBar:vertical {
    background: #202120;
    width: 16px;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical {
    background-color: #3A3A3A;
    border: 1px solid #0D0D0D;
    min-height: 24px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical:hover {
    background-color: #D84E2F;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:vertical, QScrollBar::sub-line:vertical {
    height: 0px;
    background: none;
    border: none;
}

QScrollBar::add-page:vertical, QScrollBar::sub-page:vertical {
    background: none;
}

QScrollBar:horizontal {
    background: #202120;
    height: 16px;
    border: 2px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal {
    background-color: #3A3A3A;
    border: 1px solid #0D0D0D;
    min-width: 24px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal:hover {
    background-color: #D84E2F;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:horizontal, QScrollBar::sub-line:horizontal {
    width: 0px;
    background: none;
    border: none;
}

QScrollBar::add-page:horizontal, QScrollBar::sub-page:horizontal {
    background: none;
}

QSizeGrip {
    background-color: #161616;
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
}

QToolTip {
    background-color: #202120;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    border: 2px solid #D84E2F;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 4px 6px;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Propaganda side panel (src/torrent2000/ui/widgets/propaganda_panel.py)
   -- the extra strip of window width shown only under this theme.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QWidget#cccpPropagandaPanel {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    border-left: 3px solid #D84E2F;
}

QLabel#propagandaHeader {
    color: #D84E2F;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 10pt;
}

QLabel#propagandaMessage {
    color: #F2E4C4;
    font-size: 9pt;
}

QFrame#propagandaDivider {
    background-color: #D4AF37;
    border: none;
}
